From: Kumar Bala <kumar@renovatio.systems>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DEV_Config: don't hard-fail on unrecognized /etc/issue

DEV_Equipment_Testing() refuses to run unless /etc/issue contains
"Raspbian", "Debian", or "NixOS". Yocto/Poky-built images have a
different /etc/issue despite genuinely running on Raspberry Pi
hardware, so this check produced a false negative and aborted
DEV_Module_Init() before bcm2835_init() ever ran. Warn instead of
refusing to continue.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [distro-specific check not relevant upstream]
Signed-off-by: Kumar Bala <kumar@renovatio.systems>
---
--- a/RaspberryPi_JetsonNano/c/lib/Config/DEV_Config.c
+++ b/RaspberryPi_JetsonNano/c/lib/Config/DEV_Config.c
@@ -255,10 +255,10 @@
 		}
 	}
 	if (!detected) {
-		printf("not recognized\n");
-		printf("Built for Raspberry Pi, but unable to detect environment.\n");
-		printf("Perhaps you meant to 'make JETSON' instead?\n");
-		return -1;
+		/* Yocto-built images (e.g. Poky) won't match this /etc/issue
+		 * allowlist even though they are genuinely Raspberry Pi - only
+		 * warn instead of refusing to run. */
+		printf("not recognized (continuing anyway)\n");
 	}
 #endif
 #ifdef JETSON
